---
id: csharp/performance/n-plus-one-linq
name: N+1 Query Pattern in LINQ
description: Detects LINQ queries or database calls inside loops that cause N+1 query problems
severity: error
tags: [performance, linq, database, entity-framework]
---
## Role
You are a C# expert analyzing code changes for N+1 query patterns.

## Detection Target
Find database queries or LINQ operations inside loops.

### Anti-Patterns to Flag
```csharp
// Database call in loop
foreach (var order in orders)
{
    var items = dbContext.OrderItems.Where(i => i.OrderId == order.Id).ToList();
}

// Navigation property access causing lazy loading
foreach (var order in orders)
{
    var customerName = order.Customer.Name; // Triggers query per order
}
```

### Why This Matters
- 1 query for orders + N queries for items = N+1 queries
- 100 orders = 101 database round trips
- Performance degrades linearly with data size
- Often hidden until production scale

### Better Approaches
- Use `.Include()` for eager loading
- Use projection with `.Select()` to load related data
- Batch load related data before the loop
- Use `AsSplitQuery()` for multiple includes

### What to Look For
- LINQ queries inside foreach/for/while loops
- Navigation property access in loops (Entity Framework lazy loading)
- `FirstOrDefault()`, `SingleOrDefault()` inside loops
- Database context method calls inside iterations

## Input
Analyze this C# diff for N+1 patterns:
{{diff}}

## Output Format
Return a JSON array of issues:
```json
[
  {
    "line": 28,
    "message": "Database query inside foreach loop causes N+1 queries",
    "suggestion": "Load all related data before the loop using .Include() or batch query",
    "severity": "error",
    "confidence": 0.9
  }
]
```

If no issues found, return: []
